Regenerated trolls already do far less death drops.  Troll dancing
for death drops may be the original model for pudding farming.  So
switch puddings to regenerate and that decreases the number of
death drops by puddings and thus increases the amount of work
involved.

If a corpse regenerates over the top of a live pudding, it should
dissappear or appear to merge with the live one.  Yet another way
to slightly decrease the rate of death drops.

I think the way to stop the abuse of pudding farming is to have
splits count against the extinction limit for the species.  If you
can only get 120 each of black and brown puddings, then it is
no longer possible to amass hundreds of pages of items in a
stack from the death drops.



